Phase 6 Task 6.1 (bead VieNeuTTSApp-nqx.8.1) — engine/language controls and
the Qwen install surfaces in Settings.

Delivered:
- Shared EngineProfilePicker + LanguagePicker components (new files, registered
  in qml/qmldir and qml/components/qmldir) so the synthesis tabs can reuse the
  same controls in 6.2/6.3. Language names stay native (中文, 日本語, …).
- SettingsTab cards, in order: Model family (engineProfileCard), Compute device
  (qwenDeviceCard), Qwen runtime (qwenRuntimeCard), Qwen model (qwenModelCard).
- Install / cancel / repair / remove / offline-import for the runtime and each
  checkpoint, per-state status + progress + storage, unsupported-hardware and
  platform-without-runtime refusals, corruption surfaced as repair, CPU-only
  guidance shown before any download, and open-folder targets for both trees.
- Controller: Qwen device choices + runtime/model management signals,
  properties and slots; qwenSharedBytes is manifest-derived; requiredBytes
  falls back to the pinned manifest totals pre-install; model removal passes
  real in-use / remove-shared flags.
- qwen_runtime_manifest: host_platform_tag/host_platform_key/host_devices/
  platform_label, and the device-aware default Qwen runtime manager (fixed a
  bug where the current platform key was used as a Qwen manifest key, so the
  manager was always None).

Stable objectName contract documented in SettingsTab.qml's header comment and
asserted by tests/smoke/test_ui_tabs.py scenarios settings_engine_profiles and
settings_qwen_states (Repeater delegates are re-looked-up by name, never
